# inc-7wmu: dispel must remove the standing grant and restore one copy.
# Aura and fade messages prove suppression and expiry; Will measures the grant.
# Wizard stati dumps bracket the dispel, so a lost unrelated row shows.
# Read by check_reapply_single_grant.sh. Seed 1 succeeds; seed 4 resists.
# Not seed 9: its cord armour carries a quality the same dispel suppresses,
# and that nested removal drops an unrelated row (inc-2k0c, not this bead).
# The spell targets the wearer, suppressing the item via its SS_ITEM row.
# Wait for the named fade message, rather than assuming a duration elapsed.
#
# THE DECIPHER ROLL. Reading any scroll first rolls SkillCheck(SK_DECIPHER,
# 10 + sLevel + rlm) (src/Magic.cpp:6032). A 1st-level orc barbarian has a
# tiny Decipher bonus (the passing run reads it as +1), and on this seed the
# check has failed, printing "The magic runs amok!" and spending the scroll
# with no Dispel at all -- so S4 measured nothing. The roll is staged around
# instead of fixed: the pack is stocked with several Scrolls of Dispel Magic
# (they stack) and the read is retried, bounded, until one succeeds. Success
# removes the Bloodspear's SS_ITEM row and sets the item's DISPELLED temp
# stati (src/Effects.cpp:1172), so a later successful read finds no SS_ITEM
# row left to dispel and prints no second aura; the retry therefore stops on
# the first success, leaving the "dull grey aura" line as the last message
# for the `dispelled` dump. @while bodies admit only ordinary keys, so the
# retry body names the menu letter directly: with a single readable stack the
# use menu offers it as [a] (checked in logs/screens/.../read-menu.txt).
@include chargen.keys

d
@dump:orc-sheet-without-bloodspear
ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN
SPACE                   # Auto-Identify Items
ESC

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*10                # specific weapons
@until "Sword of the Planes" DOWN
ENTER
2                       # Bloodspear's INITIAL_PLUS
ENTER
b                       # Weapon Hand
SPACE
@while "two-handed" n
s                       # stow the displaced starting weapon
@dump:orc-wielded
ESC

d
@dump:orc-sheet-with-bloodspear
ESC
# Five Scrolls of Dispel Magic, bought one at a time. They stack, so the
# pack holds one entry whose count drops with each read; the retry body below
# names the menu letter, not the count. A buy that will not stack (the first,
# with an empty pack) opens the inventory manager, whose two lines stow it and
# close; a later buy that stacks opens nothing and both lines fire zero times.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT
@until "Scroll of Dispel Magic" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
@while "In the Air':Scroll" s
@while "Ready Hand" ESC
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT
@until "Scroll of Dispel Magic" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
@while "In the Air':Scroll" s
@while "Ready Hand" ESC
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT
@until "Scroll of Dispel Magic" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
@while "In the Air':Scroll" s
@while "Ready Hand" ESC
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT
@until "Scroll of Dispel Magic" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
@while "In the Air':Scroll" s
@while "Ready Hand" ESC
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT
@until "Scroll of Dispel Magic" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
@while "In the Air':Scroll" s
@while "Ready Hand" ESC
w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
@until "Inventory:" DOWN
@dump:stati-before
@until "hObj" UP        # the next scroll view inherits this offset
ESC
# First read, then retry until the suppression aura shows. The read has two
# ways to fail on this seed: a failed Decipher roll ("The magic runs amok!")
# and, once read, an opposed caster-level check the level-10 Bloodspear can
# win ("You resist the dispelling."). Neither leaves the aura line, so a single
# @until on it retries both kinds of failure; the loop stops on the first
# success, before a second read could print a second aura. The match is "dull
# grey", not the full "dull grey aura": the message wraps at the screen edge
# and ScreenShows (src/Wposix.cpp:931) matches within one rendered row only, so
# a longer phrase that straddles the wrap is never seen. @choose is a prefix match: "(in pack) 5 Scrolls of Dispel Magic"
# names the stack with the count the five acquisitions above make, and the loop body names the
# Dispel Magic entry's letter [a]: the options fixture gives no Beginner's Kit,
# so there are no Identify scrolls (re-pinned for inc-rt8l).
r
@choose "(in pack) 5 Scrolls of Dispel Magic"
@dump:dispel-target
*
@until "dull grey" r a *
@while "Stop reading?" n
@dump:dispelled
@while "[more]" SPACE
ESC
@while "System Menu" ESC  # one message leaves no box, so ESC opened this
d
@dump:dispelled-sheet
ESC
w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
@until "Inventory:" DOWN
@dump:stati-after
@until "hObj" UP
ESC
@until "The grey glow fades" .
@dump:dispel-ended
d
@dump:restored-sheet
@quit
